---
smd: 2
title: Validation errors in spec v2
summary: Pins how a spec v2 document renders what Styled Markdown 2.0 reports as errors in every document (duplicate attributes, conflicting titles, an invalid figure kind, a Mermaid syntax error) and the removed priority of an agent block, so later releases are compared against it.
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-17
---

## Why the comments

Each case below is an error or a warning since 2.0, in every document. The comments silence them so that this document passes validation; it renders as v1 resolves each case.

## Duplicate attributes

- The last value of a key or an id is used, and a repeated class is added twice:

    <!-- smd-disable-next-line attrs/duplicate -->
    [Blue text]{color=red color=blue}, :badge[Ready]{color=red color=green}, [an anchor]{#first #second} and [a note]{.note .note}.

## Conflicting titles

<!-- smd-disable-next-line container/title-conflict -->
:::note{title="Attribute title"} Text title
The title attribute is shown; the text after the attributes is not.
:::

## An invalid figure kind

<!-- smd-disable-next-line attrs/value -->
:::figure{#fig-kind kind=tabel} Counts as a figure
A figure whose kind is not figure, table or listing is numbered as a figure: :ref[fig-kind].
:::

## Agent priority

<!-- smd-disable-next-line attrs/unknown -->
:::agent{priority=high}
Read the cases above before changing how validation reports them.
:::

## A diagram that does not parse

<!-- smd-disable mermaid/syntax -->

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A -->
```

<!-- smd-enable mermaid/syntax -->
